      "# Pakistan Wheat Support Price 2026–27: Federal Consultations Underway with Final Pricing Decision Pending",
      "## High-Level Federal Consultation on 13 October 2026\n\nIn a high-level review meeting chaired by **Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif** in Islamabad on **13 October 2026** and reported via state media (**Radio Pakistan**), the Federal Government conducted detailed deliberations on the upcoming **Rabi 2026–27 wheat cultivation campaign**.\n\nThe consultation brought together federal ministers, senior officials of the Ministry of National Food Security and Research (MNFSR), provincial agriculture representatives, and economic policy advisors to finalize the national strategy for grain self-sufficiency.",
      "> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Critical Editorial & Fact Verification Note:**\n> - **No Minimum Support Price (MSP) Announced:** The Federal Government did **NOT** fix or notify an official wheat support price per maund during the 13 October meeting.\n> - **Pricing Decision Pending:** Any final procurement price or support price requires formal approval by the **Economic Coordination Committee (ECC)** and subsequent ratification by the **Federal Cabinet**.\n> - **Do Not Trust Rumored Figures:** Social media posts claiming an approved rate of Rs. 3,900, Rs. 4,000, or Rs. 4,200 per maund are speculative and unverified by official government gazettes.\n> - **Nature of Article:** This is an informative policy briefing; it is **NOT** a citizen cash registration or farmer subsidy enrollment scheme.",
