      "## Inter-Provincial Dynamics & Procurement Policy\n\nThe fixing of the wheat support price involves delicate coordination between the federal authorities and provincial administrations (Punjab, Sindh, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, and Balochistan):\n\n- **Cost of Production Assessments:** The Agriculture Policy Institute (API) calculates comprehensive input costs—including land preparation, water, certified seed, diesel, and harvesting charges—before submitting recommendations to the ECC.\n- **Provincial Autonomy:** Following the 18th Constitutional Amendment, provincial governments retain authority to determine provincial procurement policies, highlighting the necessity for a unified federal consensus to prevent cross-border grain smuggling and price disparities.\n- **Target Production Objectives:** For the 2026–27 season, national planners aim to achieve robust acreage targets to avoid costly international commercial wheat imports.",
